On 2007-03-27, Richard Bos wrote:
> Ohle Claussen <claussen@dpi.physik.uni-goettingen.de> wrote:
>
>> On 2007-03-27, kronoman@avengingangel.us wrote:
>> > A lot of people have pointed out that there are quite a few artifacts,
>> > especially artifact weapons, that suck, and a few more that are rather
>> > mediocre. I've got here a list of ideas on how to fix this, to a
>> > point.
>
> One point against your proposal is that there are still a lot of
> artifacts that are only moderately useful; I'd still prefer Grayswandir
> or Frosty. Another is that most of the artifacts are still longswords.
> I'd like to see more good artifacts in other classes. 

Very good point. This should, IMO, in fact be the first thing to change
about the crap artifacts. More weapon class diversity is a Good Thing.

>> > Dragonbane: grants reflection when wielded.
>> 
>> Good.
>
> But it's still only a broadsword against other monsters, which is not as
> good as a longsword against the more dangerous ones, and not nearly as
> good as a proper artifact. IOW, it's still a _poor_ non-longsword
> artifact.

It would be yet another option for reflection, so in those games where you
don't aquire another source early enough, saccing for dragonbane would
become an option. Then you'd be stuck with a broadsword until you find
reflection, which is another of those lovely NetHack dilemmas that make the
game's strategy so interesting. Wouldn't happen often, of course.

>> > Snickersnee: +d5 to hit (on top of the innate +1 to hit for being a
>> > katana), +1d14 damage. IMHO, since Snickersnee is a bit harder to get
>> > than Excalibur, and has none of EX's special effects, it should be a
>> > more powerful weapon.
>> 
>> Well, something distinguishing the two might be in order, yes. Maybe a
>> special effect rather than higher numbers?
>
> I still think making Snickersnee a short sword, making the samurai quest
> artifact a katana, and making that the only combination of two artifacts
> which can be two-weaponed (and that only for a samurai) is a good idea,
> and in the spirit of the game.

The idea is very nice, but you'd have to balance two artifacts for
twoweaponing. Since twoweaponing is already _very_ powerful, that would
probably make Snick useless for everyone else.

>> > Cleaver: +d8 instead of +d6 damage, +d5 instead of +d3 to hit.
>> 
>> Wouldn't make it much more popular. It's still a battle axe, so only useful
>> to certain classes, and it's already a good early to mid game choice for
>> those.
>
> This might make it viable for barbs to keep using it right through the
> game, though (except of course in the quest..), which would be good for
> role-playing.

True.

>> > Grimtooth: bonus damage +d8 instead of +d6
>> 
>> I don't quite see the reason for this.
>
> Well, Grimtooth definitily does need a boost. It's a crappy weapon, but
> it could be an interesting choice for chaotics if it were worth
> something. It's an orcish dagger; IMO, it should be poisoned. Yeah,
